            <ArticleTitle>Prognosis of medically stabilized unstable angina pectoris with a negative exercise test.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>662-5, A6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Three hundred twenty seven patients with medically stabilized unstable angina and a negative exercise test were followed-up during a mean of 39 months. Male gender, diabetes mellitus, and previous myocardial infarction, but not exercise parameters, were predictors of death or acute myocardial infarction.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
